      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Increasing lecithin concentration likely provides more surface coverage, which can initially boost stability by creating a thicker physical barrier. However, excessive lecithin can lead to an overly packed or \"clogged\" interface, which might actually promote flocculation by bridging multiple oil droplets together. Therefore, optimizing lecithin concentration requires a balance between achieving complete surface coverage and maintaining a specific electrical repulsive force via the resulting zeta potential.",
      "source": "target",
